## ⚛️ Physics in Bug Bounty (Hardware & Signal Manipulation)
Computers are physical objects made of silicon, copper, and electricity. By exploiting physical laws, you can break software restrictions.

* 
* Rowhammer Attacks (Electromagnetic Leakage): Modern RAM chips are packed so tightly that cells can leak electrical charges to adjacent cells. By writing an exploit that rapidly reads/writes to a specific memory address, you can physically alter the bits next to it (bit-flipping). This lets you bypass software sandboxes or escalate privileges purely through electrical physics.
* Fault Injection & Voltage Glitching: By temporarily dropping the power supply (voltage) or messing with the clock speed of an IoT device or cryptographic chip at the exact microsecond a security check happens, you can induce a physical fault. The system skips the security check entirely, letting you bypass firmware locks.
* Side-Channel Analysis (SDR & Acoustics): You can use a Software Defined Radio (SDR) to capture electromagnetic radiation emitted by a computer's CPU while it processes encryption keys. Similarly, you can record the acoustic buzz of power capacitors. Advanced physics models allow you to reconstruct the secret RSA or AES keys just from these physical emissions.
