## 🧪 Chemistry in Bug Bounty (Hardware Hacking & Anti-Forensics)
Chemistry allows you to bypass physical security perimeters, reverse-engineer proprietary chips, and manipulate physical security mechanisms.

* 
* Silicon Decapping and Acid Etching: To find zero-days in a hardcoded cryptographic chip or hardware security module (HSM), you can use fuming nitric acid to dissolve the outer plastic resin package without destroying the delicate silicon die underneath. Once exposed, you can use specialized microscopes to visually trace the circuitry and extract secret keys.
* Thermal Imaging and Heat Retention: When a user types a password on a keypad or a physical keyboard, their fingers transfer heat to the buttons. If you target physical corporate environments, a thermal camera can read the heat signatures on a keypad up to a minute after they leave, showing you the exact PIN used, with the hottest button being the one pressed last.
* Tamper-Evident Bypass: Many physical servers and high-security devices are sealed with tamper-evident chemical tape or glue. Hunters specializing in physical supply-chain bugs use precise thermal controls (freezing sprays or solvents like isopropyl alcohol) to alter the chemical adhesive properties, opening the device without triggering the physical alert indicator.
