## 📐 Mathematics in Bug Bounty (Cryptanalysis, Timing, & Graph Theory)
Mathematics is the ultimate tool for finding hidden logical structures and breaking complex software protections without guessing.

* 
* Timing Attacks & Statistical Math: When a server compares an entered API key to the correct API key, it might stop checking at the first wrong character. If the first character is correct, it takes slightly longer (microseconds) to reject it. By using Bayesian statistics and analyzing thousands of timing samples, you can mathematically deduce keys character by character.
* Cryptographic Weaknesses (PRNG Deficiencies): Many web applications generate session tokens or password reset tokens using Pseudo-Random Number Generators (PRNGs). If they use weak math (like the Mersenne Twister), you can capture a few sequential tokens, use matrix math to reverse-engineer the internal state of the generator, and predict every token that will ever be generated in the future.
* Graph Theory for Network Mapping: When hunting on massive enterprise scopes (thousands of subdomains), represent the infrastructure as a mathematical graph (nodes and edges). Applying graph algorithms can highlight the path of least resistance—revealing hidden trust relationships and active directory paths that lead directly to the core network.
